<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Reading quartiles from a cumulative frequency curve</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The graph shows the cumulative frequency curve of the time, \(t\) minutes, that \({@n@}\) customers spent in a supermarket in Nakuru.</p><div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Cumulative frequency curve of the times: the points ({#jx[1]#}, {#jy[1]#}), ({#jx[2]#}, {#jy[2]#}), ({#jx[3]#}, {#jy[3]#}), ({#jx[4]#}, {#jy[4]#}), ({#jx[5]#}, {#jy[5]#}), ({#jx[6]#}, {#jy[6]#}) and ({#jx[7]#}, {#jy[7]#}) joined by straight lines. Horizontal axis time in minutes, with a small square for each minute; vertical axis cumulative frequency, with a small square for every {#dy#} customers.">
[[jsxgraph width="560px" height="400px"]]
(function() {
  var jx = {#jx#};
  var jy = {#jy#};
  var x0 = {#xmin#};
  var x1 = {#xmax#};
  var n = {#n#};
  var dy = {#dy#};
  var sx = x1 - x0;
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
    boundingbox: [x0 - 0.09*sx, 1.12*n, x1 + 0.03*sx, -0.13*n],
    axis: false, grid: false, pan: {enabled: false}, zoom: {enabled: false},
    showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false
  });
  // small squares: 1 minute across, dy customers up; thicker lines every 10 minutes and every 5*dy
  var gx, iy;
  for (gx = x0; gx <= x1; gx += 1) {
    b.create('segment', [[gx, 0], [gx, n]], {strokeColor: ((gx - x0) % 10 === 0) ? '#a8a8a8' : '#e2e2e2', strokeWidth: ((gx - x0) % 10 === 0) ? 1 : 0.5, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  }
  for (iy = 0; iy <= 20; iy += 1) {
    b.create('segment', [[x0, iy*dy], [x1, iy*dy]], {strokeColor: (iy % 5 === 0) ? '#a8a8a8' : '#e2e2e2', strokeWidth: (iy % 5 === 0) ? 1 : 0.5, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  }
  b.create('segment', [[x0, 0], [x1, 0]], {strokeColor: '#000000', strokeWidth: 1.5, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  b.create('segment', [[x0, 0], [x0, n]], {strokeColor: '#000000', strokeWidth: 1.5, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  for (gx = x0; gx <= x1; gx += 10) {
    b.create('text', [gx, -0.04*n, String(gx)], {anchorX: 'middle', anchorY: 'middle', fixed: true, highlight: false, fontSize: 12});
  }
  for (iy = 0; iy <= 20; iy += 5) {
    b.create('text', [x0 - 0.012*sx, iy*dy, String(iy*dy)], {anchorX: 'right', anchorY: 'middle', fixed: true, highlight: false, fontSize: 12});
  }
  b.create('text', [x0 + sx/2, -0.1*n, 'Time (minutes)'], {anchorX: 'middle', anchorY: 'middle', fixed: true, highlight: false, fontSize: 13});
  b.create('text', [x0 + 0.01*sx, 1.07*n, 'Cumulative frequency'], {anchorX: 'left', anchorY: 'middle', fixed: true, highlight: false, fontSize: 13});
  var pts = [];
  for (var i = 0; i < jx.length; i++) {
    pts.push(b.create('point', [jx[i], jy[i]], {name: '', size: 2, face: 'o', strokeColor: '#1f4e9c', fillColor: '#1f4e9c', fixed: true, highlight: false, showInfobox: false}));
  }
  b.create('polygonalchain', pts, {borders: {strokeColor: '#1f4e9c', strokeWidth: 2, highlight: false}, fixed: true});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div><p>Use the graph. Read each value to the nearest minute.</p><p>(a) Estimate the median time.</p><div>Median \(=\) [[input:ans1]] minutes [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Estimate the lower quartile, \(Q_1\).</p><div>\(Q_1 =\) [[input:ans2]] minutes [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Estimate the upper quartile, \(Q_3\).</p><div>\(Q_3 =\) [[input:ans3]] minutes [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div><p>(d) Estimate the interquartile range.</p><div>IQR \(=\) [[input:ans4]] minutes [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div><p>(e) Estimate the quartile deviation.</p><div>QD \(=\) [[input:ans5]] minutes [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt5]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>To read a quartile, go across from its position on the cumulative frequency axis to the curve, then down to the time axis. With \(n = {@n@}\), the positions are \(n/4 = {@n/4@}\), \(n/2 = {@n/2@}\) and \(3n/4 = {@3*n/4@}\). The graph is made of straight segments, so each reading equals the value from the formula \(L + \dfrac{\text{position} - CF}{F} \times c\).</p><p>(a) Across from \({@n/2@}\): median \(\approx {@medd@}\) minutes. (b) Across from \({@n/4@}\): \(Q_1 \approx {@q1d@}\) minutes. (c) Across from \({@3*n/4@}\): \(Q_3 \approx {@q3d@}\) minutes.</p><p>(d) The interquartile range is the spread of the middle half of the data: \(Q_3 - Q_1 \approx {@iqrd@}\) minutes.</p><p>(e) The quartile deviation is half of it: \((Q_3 - Q_1)/2 \approx {@qdd@}\) minutes. Answers within about a minute of these are accepted (two minutes for the IQR, which uses two readings).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
